      "message": "Non Protected VM with re-signed images with different key should ideally boot.\n\nThis test (testBootSucceedsWhenNonProtectedVmStartsWithImagesSignedWithDifferentKey) fails  resigning the the apexes was changing the vbmeta partition, which changes the vbmeta hash. Vbmeta hashes are part of bootconfigs \u0026 early userspace will fail to verify the system/vendor partition, causing the boot fail.\n\nIdeally, SignVirtApex() should sign initrd/kernel and NEED NOT sign super image (system/vendor). This is in scope of b/245277660.\n\nAlternatively, we can change the logic of re-signing here. SignVirtApex() on signing could update the bootconfigs with new vbmeta hash related values (bootconfigs are are appended in initrd). Though will pass the test \u0026 but is a bit unnecessary considering we need not sign the system/vendor img at all. \n\nThis is in scope of",
